WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.900
The third question needs no model.

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.400
Dates are what models make up most.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.600
Two changelogs. The same shape.

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.500
A date, and then a heading.

5
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.200
One sentence needs care.

6
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.900
A promise about August, not a release.

7
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.900
So the line has to be a date.

8
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.200
Not contain one. Start with one.

9
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.200
Four changes in ninety days.

10
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.600
And seventy on the page. Say both.

11
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.600
One page had no dates at all.

12
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.100
Which is not the same as no changes.

13
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.100
A podcast episode became a product change.

14
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.600
An article is not a section answer.

15
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.200
And a shorter URL beat the changelog.

16
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.600
A date is checkable. So we never guess one.
